KG42.register("rules-93fb9113037f43898b2526d1",{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Each supply bid specifies an energy carrier, delivery-hour, supply status and network injection location, and states one quantity and one valuation. Scope: Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply bids follow the full trading-horizon submission schedule, with separate bids for separate delivery periods; this does not prescribe that every hour's bid must be a supply bid. Scope: Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. Agents are allowed to update their supply bids between market clearings. Scope: Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation. Condition: Between successive market clearings. Supply bids are submitted once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. Scope: Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. Condition: The described schedule assumes 1 h time-periods; the design permits longer or shorter periods. Agents may submit multiple supply bids with different quantities and valuations to construct a step-function curve without using bid dependencies. Scope: Permitted construction of supply bid curves. Condition: When constructing a step-function bid curve. Agents cannot submit indivisible supply bids that must be either fully accepted or rejected entirely. Scope: Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. Supply bids in one hour cannot be conditioned on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing. Scope: Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. Condition: Conditioning a bid in one hour on another hour's outcome within the same clearing.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Permitted construction of supply bid curves. | Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. | Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. | Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. | Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. | Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. | Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E25"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each supply bid specifies an energy carrier, delivery-hour, supply status and network injection location, and states one quantity and one valuation. Scope: Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E015"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids follow the full trading-horizon submission schedule, with separate bids for separate delivery periods; this does not prescribe that every hour's bid must be a supply bid. Scope: Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E014"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents are allowed to update their supply bids between market clearings. Scope: Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation. Condition: Between successive market clearings.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E014"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids are submitted once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. Scope: Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. Condition: The described schedule assumes 1 h time-periods; the design permits longer or shorter periods.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents may submit multiple supply bids with different quantities and valuations to construct a step-function curve without using bid dependencies. Scope: Permitted construction of supply bid curves. Condition: When constructing a step-function bid curve.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E020"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents cannot submit indivisible supply bids that must be either fully accepted or rejected entirely. Scope: Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids in one hour cannot be conditioned on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing. Scope: Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. Condition: Conditioning a bid in one hour on another hour's outcome within the same clearing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E25"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to minimize forecast errors, bid submission and market clearing take place as close to the delivery-hour as possible. Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. However, for the market to be able to accommodate dependencies over longer periods of time, each market clearing also includes a range of future hours. The full range of hours included in a market clearing is referred to as the trading horizon. The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are 4. allow","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E020","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids qb • should be greater than or equal","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Note that agents can construct some bid combinations without the need to use bid dependencies. For example, step-function bid curves can be built by simply submitting multiple bids with different quantities and valuations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.1. The indivisibility issue","anchor_text":"producer may have a minimum load requirement such that it has to either be turned oﬀor operate above","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"As described in 4.2, the market optimization problem is linear and no integer variables are introduced. This means that there is no possibility for agents to submit indivisible bids, i.e. bids that should be either fully accepted or not accepted at all."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.3. Multiple energy carriers and flexibility instruments","anchor_text":"to Even though the proposed ﬂexibility instruments provide a vast list le of options and possibiliti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"Even though the proposed flexibility instruments provide a vast list of options and possibilities, there are limitations in what they can represent. For example, since agents cannot submit indivisible bids, the possibility for a market participant to completely switch between electricity and DH cannot be ensured, i.e. it cannot be ensured that only one of these options exclusively will be cleared. Another limitation is the difficulty to construct bids for energy storage that takes full advantage of the flexibility offered by such assets. Although it is possible to construct bids and bid dependencies that represent a specific charge and discharge cycle, it is difficult to fully capture all possibilities and constraints of a typical energy storage. Accurately capturing all possible charge and discharge possibilities over a trading horizon would require a very large number of bids and bid dependencies. Further, the available capacity for hours further out in the horizon depends on the amount cleared in prior hours. However, it is not possible to condition the bids in one hour on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The frozen rule is procedural/admission: it governs what a supply bid contains, when it is submitted or updated, and what bid forms are inadmissible. It does not define a design-selection or operational decision variable in this graph. The sole graph member is bidding.supply; no edge or variable node is present.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameters or numerical values are specified by this frozen supply-submission rule. Bid quantity and valuation are submitted per-bid data, and the 1 h time-period is an illustrative assumption in the source for the broader rolling-horizon design, not a fixed parameter of a formal supply-submission equation here. No domain or value is asserted."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","quote":"Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","quote":"Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","quote":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","quote":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","quote":"For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","quote":"Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E020","quote":"Note that agents can construct some bid combinations without the need to use bid dependencies. For example, step-function bid curves can be built by simply submitting multiple bids with different quantities and valuations."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","quote":"This means that there is no possibility for agents to submit indivisible bids, i.e. bids that should be either fully accepted or not accepted at all."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E25","quote":"However, it is not possible to condition the bids in one hour on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"29e8125b5976355d1b1e82d33e275389b5f51a470ba9d07071db60b6fc44894c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"Frozen rule v141-c-R002 is a bidding-stage procedural/admission rule for supply bids. Its seven constraints specify bid content, trading-horizon submission and update timing, step-function curve construction, and admissibility limits (no indivisible supply bids; no cross-hour outcome conditioning). The only frozen graph member is the unary node bidding.supply and there are no edges; the source does not present an optimization objective or parameterized equation for supply submission in this rule. Therefore the rule is treated as non-mathematical, with no x/theta objects and no formalized phi expressions; this is not a claim that the paper lacks variables elsewhere.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
